«
@@ DMOTPower — demo of the power of TTest1: ten values drawn from a
@@ normal law of mean 10.5 and standard deviation 1, tested against
@@ μ₀ = 10. H₀ is false, yet with ten values the shift of half a
@@ standard deviation is detected only about three presses in ten.
@@ Author & design          : Jean Wilson
@@ Co-authors & programming  : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
  10 0 0
  → dtn dt1 dt2
  «
    1 dtn For dti
      10.5 1 ⓁNormlRand
      Dup dt1 + 'dt1' Store Sq dt2 + 'dt2' Store
    Next
    dt1 dtn / dt2 dt1 Sq dtn / - dtn 1 - / √
    → dtm dts
    «
      dtm "mean" →Tag dts "s" →Tag
      dtn dtm dts 10 ⓁTTest1
      Dup DeleteTag 0.05 < "H₀ rejected: the shift is detected" "H₀ kept: the shift is missed" IFTE "verdict" →Tag
    »
  »
»
